 "05/17/2025", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This is a course designed to intermediate students to enhance their oral and written communication skills in Portuguese while engaging a broad range of topics related to Afro-Luso-Brazilian culture. Along with the textbook, students will read a short-essay book, be exposed to a number of films and critically reflect and discuss the films and readings. Students will continue to build their knowledge on grammar and vocabulary as well as Global Portuguese culture and language diversity.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "Satisfies Option 1.", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "Although most of the materials are geared to speakers of Spanish, speakers of other romance languages, such as French, Italian, or Catalan, etc. will also find this course effective as an introduction to Portuguese.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite:\u00a0PORT 2010.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2895, "crseId": 360060, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "PORT", "catalogNbr": "2800", "titleShort": "Perspectives on Brazil", "titleLong": "Perspectives on Brazil", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 17794, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "12:20PM", "timeEnd": "01:10PM", "startDt": "01/21/2025", "endDt": "05/06/2025", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "dmo67", "firstName": "Denise", "middleName": "Maria", "lastName": "Osborne"}], "pattern": "MWF", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Conducted in English."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/21/2025", "endDt": "05/17/2025", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "C", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "LATA", "catalogNbr": "2800", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/21/2025", "sessionEndDt": "05/17/2025", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This course provides an introduction and overview of Brazilian culture. It will study different periods of Brazilian history, through the analysis of films, literature, essays, visual arts, and music. Students will explore different definitions of Brazilian identity and \"Brazilianness\" focusing on key topics including the formation of the colonial Brazil and the emergence of the nation of Brazil as a tropical paradise; slavery and abolition; the particularities century; and the contradictions of the modernization process throughout the 20th century. We will consider elements of Brazilian popular culture such as Carnival, Samba, and \"telenovels,\" and some of the most important cultural movements of the 20th century, such as \"Modernismo,\" \"Cinema Novo,\" and \"Tropicalia.\" The primary objective of the course is to provide students with the relevant background to understand Brazilian cultural history.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": "(GLC-AS, SCD-AS) (CA-AG, D-AG)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "cata